gufo (0.18.0-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Filesystem hardening on both units: ProtectSystem=full, ProtectHome=yes, PrivateTmp=yes and one
    explicit ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/gufo. The set was derived by measuring what the running instance
    actually holds open -- file descriptors under /var/lib/huggingface (read-only mmaps of the weights)
    and /var/lib/gufo/cache/instances/<instance> (the disk cache the launcher mkdirs) -- plus a grep of
    the shipped env files (zero /home references) and of the launcher (no /tmp, no writes under /usr).
  * Not set, on purpose: ProtectSystem=strict, ProtectKernelTunables, NoNewPrivileges. Three source
    files read /sys for device information and the ROCm kfd/dri access path has not been proven under a
    read-only /sys or a no-new-privileges domain. The failure mode of those three is a unit that will
    not start, which costs a full model reload -- a larger outage than the exposure they remove. Widen
    only with a cold start and a real completion measured under each one, on real hardware.
  * /run/gufo is deliberately absent from ReadWritePaths: ProtectSystem=full does not make /run
    read-only, so granting it would be decoration. The markers there are written by root during dpkg,
    not by the service process.
  * systemd-analyze verify: no findings on either unit.

 -- Gufo Maintainers <maintainers@gufo.dev>  Mon, 20 Oct 2026 10:20:00 +0000

gufo (0.18.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rebased onto upstream main at 2caf2a82. Upstream did NOT tag a new release for this:
    version.txt is still 0.18.0 and v0.18.0 remains the newest tag, so the seven commits it
    published ride under the same upstream version. The revision exists precisely to keep the
    mapping honest -- one version string, one set of bytes -- because 0.18.0-1 was built from a
    different commit (d1830de7) and is still on disk next to this one.
  * Upstream content picked up by this rebuild: greedy MTP drafts priced at the decoding
    occupancy (#664), sampled requests using the small MTP draft head on multi-session
    (#673), q8_1 block sum stored as d*sum(q) (#667), /props reporting model, build, context,
    sessions and vision (#669), batched greedy DSpark frontier stopping before an accepted EOS
    (#668), plus docs and functional-suite adjustments.
  * Packaging is unchanged from 0.18.0-1 apart from this entry: same maintainer scripts, same
    units, same conffiles.

