 -- Gufo Maintainers <maintainers@gufo.dev>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:35:00 +0000

gufo (0.17.1-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Lifecycle correctness, found in production and then audited end to end:
    - An upgrade from a package whose prerm marked with an empty file now restores the
      instance. The marker format is versioned: releases before this one wrote a zero-byte
      marker, which proved nothing to the read side, so a running service was left down after
      the upgrade and the message said no unit existed. Proven by scenarios 18 and 19 of the
      shipped autopkgtest, which now generate legacy-shaped input instead of only current-shaped.
    - daemon-reload runs BEFORE units are restarted, so a restart uses the new unit definition
      rather than the manager's cached copy of the old one.
    - A unit that fails to restore now exits the maintainer script non-zero: a failed restart is
      reported to dpkg and to the caller, not printed as a warning on a green run.
    - The shared model cache is no longer chowned by this package. If it already exists, the
      service joins the group that owns it instead of taking the directory.
  * Units: the classic unit and its instances now conflict (same launcher, same default port);
    a crash loop can no longer reload the resident model without bound (StartLimit*), and the
    start timeout is pinned above the measured cold-load time instead of systemd's 90 s default.
  * Prerm: stops units with systemctl when deb-systemd-invoke is absent, instead of doing
    nothing and replacing the binary underneath a running process.
  * Provenance: get-revision.sh ignores non-release tags, so a backup tag can no longer become
    a shipped version string; gen-changelog.sh refuses to write a downgrade without an explicit
    opt-in; postrm refreshes the loader cache and hands kept state to root rather than leaving
    it owned by a deleted uid.
  * Packaging: the lifecycle autopkgtest is now discoverable (Testsuite: autopkgtest in the
    source stanza) and the ROCm apt pin is scoped to ROCm package families rather than
    `Package: *'.
  * Deploy tools: installation is non-interactive with confold, detects a silently-skipped
    install ("0 upgraded"), and verifies the running process and its binary inode rather than
    the package database. The model cache sync checks free space and a live server on the target
    before touching anything, and repairs ownership only on the paths it moved.

 -- Gufo Maintainers <maintainers@gufo.dev>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0000

